# /.dockerignore — the repo root.
#
# ================================================================================================
# THIS FILE IS NOT DEAD WEIGHT: IT IS THE ONLY .dockerignore THAT APPLIES TO apps/web AND
# apps/widget, AND WITHOUT IT THOSE TWO BUILDS HAD NO EXCLUSION AT ALL.
# ================================================================================================
# No image in this repo uses the repo root as its PRIMARY build context. That is deliberate — see
# the header of apps/web/Dockerfile. But both web images take the repo root as a NAMED build
# context (`workspace`, declared in compose.yaml), and every one of their COPY lines reads
# `--from=workspace`. Their own apps/{web,widget}/.dockerignore files each describe themselves as
# "authoritative for the PRIMARY build context" — which is true, and also means they were
# filtering a context that neither Dockerfile ever copies a single byte from.
#
# BuildKit applies a local named context's OWN root .dockerignore to that context (verified
# empirically, not assumed: a file matched here does not appear in the destination). So this file
# is the exclusion list for `workspace`, and until it existed the entire repository — .git,
# infrastructure/docker/secrets/, every developer .env, every Playwright storage-state file — was
# uploaded to the daemon on every `docker compose build web`.
#
# A layer is permanent. Deleting a file in a later RUN does not remove it from the earlier layer;
# `docker history` and `docker save` both still show it, and anyone who can pull the image can
# read it.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* EXCLUDED: test sources (`tests/`, `*.spec.ts`, `*.test.ts`,
# playwright.config.ts). apps/web/tsconfig.json includes `**/*.ts`, so `next build` type-checks
# them; excluding them here would make the image build a WEAKER check than CI's
# `pnpm --filter web typecheck` and let a type error reach main through the image. Test
# ARTIFACTS — which hold real cookies and tokens — are excluded below.

# ================================================================================================
# SECRETS. Nothing below this heading may ever enter a build context.
# ================================================================================================
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!*.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
id_rsa*

# The Compose secret files themselves: KEK, both internal HMAC signing keys, the database and
# Valkey passwords, the S3 secret. They reach a container through `secrets:` at RUN time and must
# never reach one at BUILD time.
infrastructure/docker/secrets/

# Playwright storage state is a real authenticated session for the test users.
**/playwright/.auth/
**/.auth/

# ================================================================================================
# VERSION CONTROL AND AGENT STATE
# ================================================================================================
# .git carries every deleted file and every rewritten commit — including anything a secret scan
# has already caught and someone "removed" in a later commit.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.claude/
.github/

# ================================================================================================
# DEPENDENCIES AND BUILD OUTPUT — rebuilt inside the image, from the lockfiles
# ================================================================================================
# A host node_modules copied in would shadow the frozen install with whatever the developer's
# machine resolved, silently, and the image would contain packages in no SBOM and no lockfile.
**/node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
**/.next/
**/out/
**/dist/
**/.turbo/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/vendor/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/

# ================================================================================================
# TEST AND COVERAGE ARTIFACTS (not test sources — see the header)
# ================================================================================================
**/playwright-report/
**/blob-report/
**/test-results/
**/coverage/
**/.nyc_output/

# ================================================================================================
# MODEL WEIGHTS AND LARGE FIXTURES — never in a layer
# ================================================================================================
# Gigabytes each, in no SBOM, invisible to pip-audit, and carrying their own licences. They arrive
# on a mounted volume pinned by commit SHA in models.manifest.toml.
**/models/
*.safetensors
*.gguf
*.onnx

# ================================================================================================
# DOCS AND EDITOR NOISE — no image reads these
# ================================================================================================
docs/
KnowledgeBot-AI.md
*.log
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
